From: EglantinePS5
Subject: [PATCH] up: EDEN_UP_DRAIN_AT_AREA=1: an area change drains at once whatever waits, and opens a 20 s window in which a short pool drains with 16 MiB of deleted buffers waiting, 100 ms apart; off by default

Switches: EDEN_UP_DRAIN_AT_AREA=1 (exact). Numbers (digits, else the default):
_GROW_MIB=<MiB> allocator growth since the last frame end or area drain that means a burst (384),
_DROP_MIB=<MiB> deleted buffers waiting with the pool not short that mean the old area goes (192),
_PENDING_MIB=<MiB> worth a drain in the window with the pool short (16), _MS=<ms> window (20000),
_GAP_MS=<ms> shortest time between drains at a burst or in the window (100). Acts with
EDEN_UP_PRESSURE_DRAIN=1 (in a frame too) or 2 (frame ends only). Outside the window the drain is
unchanged (EDEN_UP_PRESSURE_DRAIN_PENDING_MIB and _GAP_MS).
Lines (stderr): "EDEN_UP_DRAIN_AT_AREA on: ..." once; "EDEN_UP_DRAIN_AT_AREA window <n> opened
(<why>): allocator use ..., deleted buffers waiting ..., largest free piece ..."; "EDEN_UP_DRAIN_AT_AREA
drain <n> (drain <m>, at a burst|in the window): ... freed, ... staging; deleted buffers before ...;
largest free piece before ..." (the first 64).

Why: with PENDING_MIB=256 the 13 Nov loads drained only when 923-947 MiB of deleted buffers waited
and the pool was already short: run1395's drain 1 came after the 297 MiB depth image and its 288
MiB staging upload (320 MiB of staging freed by it, largest free piece 8 MiB at the look, RADV
available 5 MiB at t_s 191, stderr 860/902), run1397's before them (11 MiB staging, 239 MiB, stderr
1157); 21 and 6 looks were skipped for "too little waiting" (stderr 982, 1213). The buffer cache's
drop (425-439 MiB of deleted buffers waiting with 634-920 MiB in one piece, run1397 stderr 1136,
run1395 stderr 848) came 3-11 s before the image burst; in the field the 10 s peaks were 1-54 MiB.

What (RasterizerVulkan::PressureDrainLook): (a) the allocator's use (UsedBytes) grew by _GROW_MIB
since the last frame-end look or area drain, or (b) the census's area count moved
(MemoryCensus::NoteArea, EDEN_UP_MEM_CENSUS=1): a drain at once, past the pending mark and the
short-pool test (the gap, the GPU-behind tick and conditional rendering still hold); it frees the
staging pool's finished uploads and the deleted images too. (a), (b), or (c) _DROP_MIB of deleted
buffers waiting while the pool is not short (no drain by itself) open or extend the window.
With EDEN_UP_DRAIN_TO_POOL=1 buffers get memory of their own for the window (0896).
Cost: at a burst one flush and a GPU wait of at most EDEN_UP_PRESSURE_DRAIN_MS (80) per drain, at
most every 100 ms, in frames that take seconds; nothing in the field unless the pool is short or
the allocator grows 384 MiB within a frame. Off: one test of a static per look.

Translation id: vk_rasterizer.cpp and pressure_drain.h are not in gen-translation-id.py's inputs;
the names are not in TranslationSwitches (EDEN_NX2_AREA_EVICT, which is, is not read): KEEPS THE
STORE.

---
diff --git a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/pressure_drain.h b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/pressure_drain.h
index 80bb39be59..31899a373a 100644
--- a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/pressure_drain.h
+++ b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/pressure_drain.h
@@ -130,6 +130,74 @@ struct Config {
     return config;
 }
 
+/// EDEN_UP_DRAIN_AT_AREA=1 (exact "1"; off unless set; acts with EDEN_UP_PRESSURE_DRAIN=1 or 2).
+///
+/// At the load past the field the drain waited for EDEN_UP_PRESSURE_DRAIN_PENDING_MIB (256) of
+/// deleted buffers with the pool already short, so its first drain came when the new area had
+/// taken the pool: in one start after the 297 MiB depth image and its 288 MiB staging upload were
+/// in (320 MiB of staging freed by that drain, the pool's largest piece 8 MiB at the look), in the
+/// other before them (11 MiB of staging, 239 MiB). With this switch an area change opens a window:
+///
+///   - signals: (a) the allocator's use grew by _GROW_MIB (384) or more since the last frame end or
+///     area drain (a burst of new images and buffers, seen inside the long load frame); (b) the
+///     census noted an image burst (EDEN_UP_MEM_CENSUS's own count of AREA_EVICT's burst: 100 new
+///     images in 30 frames, seen at a frame end); (c) _DROP_MIB (192) or more of deleted buffers
+///     waiting while the pool is not short (the buffer cache letting the old area go: 425-439 MiB
+///     3-11 s before the image burst in the 13 Nov starts; at most 54 MiB in any 10 s of the field).
+///   - (a) and (b) drain at once, whatever waits and however much room the pool has, at most every
+///     _GAP_MS (100): the staging pool's finished uploads and the deleted images go too.
+///   - for _MS (20000) after the last signal, with the pool short, a drain needs only _PENDING_MIB
+///     (16) of deleted buffers, at most every _GAP_MS. Outside the window: PENDING_MIB, as before.
+///   - with EDEN_UP_DRAIN_TO_POOL=1, new buffers get memory of their own for the window.
+///
+/// Lines: EDEN_UP_DRAIN_AT_AREA (each window opened, and each drain it made, the first 64), and the
+/// drain's own lines.
+struct AreaConfig {
+    bool on;
+    u64 grow;    ///< Bytes of allocator growth that mean a burst
+    u64 drop;    ///< Bytes of deleted buffers that mean the old area goes
+    u64 pending; ///< Bytes worth a drain inside the window with the pool short
+    std::chrono::milliseconds window;
+    std::chrono::milliseconds gap;
+};
+
+[[nodiscard]] inline const AreaConfig& GetAreaConfig() {
+    static const AreaConfig config = [] {
+        AreaConfig c{};
+        const char* const value = std::getenv("EDEN_UP_DRAIN_AT_AREA");
+        c.on = value != nullptr && std::strcmp(value, "1") == 0;
+        c.grow = EnvNumber("EDEN_UP_DRAIN_AT_AREA_GROW_MIB", 384, 32, 65535) << 20;
+        c.drop = EnvNumber("EDEN_UP_DRAIN_AT_AREA_DROP_MIB", 192, 16, 65535) << 20;
+        c.pending = EnvNumber("EDEN_UP_DRAIN_AT_AREA_PENDING_MIB", 16, 1, 65535) << 20;
+        c.window = std::chrono::milliseconds{
+            EnvNumber("EDEN_UP_DRAIN_AT_AREA_MS", 20000, 1000, 600000)};
+        c.gap = std::chrono::milliseconds{EnvNumber("EDEN_UP_DRAIN_AT_AREA_GAP_MS", 100, 10, 60000)};
+        if (c.on) {
+            std::fprintf(stderr,
+                         "EDEN_UP_DRAIN_AT_AREA on: a burst is %llu MiB of allocator growth or a "
+                         "census area note, the old area going is %llu MiB of deleted buffers; "
+                         "%lld ms window, %llu MiB worth a drain in it, %lld ms apart\n",
+                         static_cast<unsigned long long>(c.grow >> 20),
+                         static_cast<unsigned long long>(c.drop >> 20),
+                         static_cast<long long>(c.window.count()),
+                         static_cast<unsigned long long>(c.pending >> 20),
+                         static_cast<long long>(c.gap.count()));
+        }
+        return c;
+    }();
+    return config;
+}
+
+/// EDEN_UP_DRAIN_AT_AREA's state, the recording thread's.
+struct AreaState {
+    u64 baseline{};  ///< Allocator use at the last frame end or area drain (0: not read yet)
+    u32 census_notes{};
+    bool census_seen{};
+    std::chrono::steady_clock::time_point until{}; ///< The window's end
+    u64 windows{};
+    u64 drains{};
+};
+
 /// The pool's largest free piece (the front's kernel query), 0 where it is not known.
 [[nodiscard]] inline u64 LargestFree() {
     return VideoCommon::MemoryCensus::FreeLargest();
@@ -167,6 +235,7 @@ struct State {
     u64 total_drains{};
     u64 total_freed{};
     Counts counts{};
+    AreaState area{}; ///< EDEN_UP_DRAIN_AT_AREA
 };
 
 /// The recording thread's (the split's back) only.
diff --git a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_rasterizer.cpp b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_rasterizer.cpp
index 79cd71ea0a..ed83ad177c 100644
--- a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_rasterizer.cpp
+++ b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_rasterizer.cpp
@@ -3208,21 +3208,69 @@ void RasterizerVulkan::PressureDrainLook(bool frame_end) {
     }
     const bool refused = s.refusal_pending;
     const bool short_pool = largest != 0 && largest < config.pool_mark;
+    // EDEN_UP_DRAIN_AT_AREA=1 (pressure_drain.h, AreaConfig): an area change drains at once and
+    // opens a window in which a short pool drains with little waiting.
+    const PD::AreaConfig& area = PD::GetAreaConfig();
+    bool burst = false;
+    bool area_open = false;
+    if (area.on) [[unlikely]] {
+        PD::AreaState& a = s.area;
+        const u64 used_now = memory_allocator.UsedBytes();
+        const char* why = nullptr;
+        if (a.baseline != 0 && used_now >= a.baseline + area.grow) {
+            burst = true;
+            why = "the allocator grew";
+        }
+        const u32 notes =
+            VideoCommon::MemoryCensus::Get().area_notes.load(std::memory_order_acquire);
+        if (a.census_seen && notes != a.census_notes) {
+            burst = true;
+            why = why != nullptr ? why : "the census saw an image burst";
+        }
+        a.census_notes = notes;
+        a.census_seen = true;
+        const bool drop = !burst && !short_pool && waiting.second >= area.drop;
+        if (burst || drop) {
+            if (now >= a.until) {
+                ++a.windows;
+                std::fprintf(stderr,
+                             "EDEN_UP_DRAIN_AT_AREA window %llu opened (%s): allocator use %llu "
+                             "MiB (%llu at the last frame end or area drain), deleted buffers "
+                             "waiting %zu, %llu MiB, largest free piece %llu MiB\n",
+                             static_cast<unsigned long long>(a.windows),
+                             why != nullptr ? why : "deleted buffers of the old area",
+                             PD::Mib(used_now), PD::Mib(a.baseline), waiting.first,
+                             PD::Mib(waiting.second), PD::Mib(largest));
+            }
+            a.until = now + area.window;
+            if (DrainToPool::OwnMemoryOn()) {
+                DrainToPool::Arm(static_cast<s64>(area.window.count()));
+            }
+        }
+        if (frame_end || a.baseline == 0) {
+            a.baseline = used_now;
+        }
+        area_open = now < a.until;
+    }
     // EDEN_UP_DRAIN_TO_POOL=1 (vulkan_common/drain_to_pool.h): new buffers get memory of their own
     // for the next 3 s while the pool is short or memory was refused.
     if (DrainToPool::OwnMemoryOn() && (short_pool || refused)) [[unlikely]] {
         DrainToPool::Arm(3000);
     }
-    if (!refused && !short_pool) {
+    if (!refused && !short_pool && !burst) {
         line();
         return;
     }
-    if (!refused && waiting.second < config.pending_mark) {
+    const u64 pending_mark = area_open ? area.pending : config.pending_mark;
+    if (!refused && !burst && waiting.second < pending_mark) {
         ++c.nothing;
         line();
         return;
     }
-    const auto gap = refused ? config.gap / 4 : config.gap;
+    auto gap = refused ? config.gap / 4 : config.gap;
+    if (burst || area_open) {
+        gap = (std::min)(gap, std::chrono::duration_cast<decltype(gap)>(area.gap));
+    }
     if (s.last_drain != std::chrono::steady_clock::time_point{} && now - s.last_drain < gap) {
         ++c.skipped_gap;
         line();
@@ -3327,6 +3375,21 @@ void RasterizerVulkan::PressureDrainLook(bool frame_end) {
         to_pool_seen.largest_after = PD::LargestFree();
         PD::ToPoolLine(s.total_drains, freed, largest, to_pool_seen);
     }
+    if (burst || area_open) [[unlikely]] {
+        PD::AreaState& a = s.area;
+        // The next burst is growth past what this drain left.
+        a.baseline = after;
+        if (++a.drains <= 64) {
+            std::fprintf(stderr,
+                         "EDEN_UP_DRAIN_AT_AREA drain %llu (drain %llu, %s): %llu MiB freed, "
+                         "%llu MiB of it staging; deleted buffers before: %zu, %llu MiB; largest "
+                         "free piece before %llu MiB\n",
+                         static_cast<unsigned long long>(a.drains),
+                         static_cast<unsigned long long>(s.total_drains),
+                         burst ? "at a burst" : "in the window", PD::Mib(freed), PD::Mib(staging),
+                         waiting.first, PD::Mib(waiting.second), PD::Mib(largest));
+        }
+    }
     if (s.total_drains <= 16 || s.total_drains % 64 == 0) {
         std::fprintf(stderr,
                      "EDEN_UP_PRESSURE_DRAIN %llu %s%s: waited %llu ms, %s; %llu MiB freed "
